@startuml backend-classes
!pragma layout smetana
title Backend class diagram - HTTP, application service and composition

left to right direction
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0

package "HTTP layer (api)" {
  class MachineController <<Spring REST controller>> {
    +state(): MachineView
    +insertCredit(request): MachineView
    +returnCredit(): ReturnedCreditResponse
    +purchase(request): PurchaseResult
    +refill(request): MachineView
  }
  class MachineExceptionHandler <<Spring advice>> {
    +handleMachineException(...): ProblemDetail
    +handleValidationException(...): ProblemDetail
    +handleUnreadableBody(...): ProblemDetail
  }
  class InsertCreditRequest <<validated record>> {
    amount: BigDecimal
  }
  class PositionsRequest <<validated record>> {
    items: List<CartItemRequest>
  }
  class CartItemRequest <<validated record>> {
    productId: long
    quantity: int
  }
  class ReturnedCreditResponse <<record>> {
    returned: BigDecimal
  }
}

package "Application and domain" {
  class MachineService <<Spring service>> {
    -machine: VendingMachine
    +view(): MachineView
    +insertCoin(amount): MachineView
    +returnCredit(): BigDecimal
    +purchase(lines): PurchaseResult
    +refill(lines): MachineView
  }
  class VendingMachine <<domain aggregate>> {
    -products: Map<Long, Product>
    -stock: Map<Long, Integer>
    -credit: BigDecimal
    -totalRevenue: BigDecimal
    +view(): MachineView
    +insertCoin(amount): MachineView
    +returnCredit(): BigDecimal
    +purchase(lines): PurchaseResult
    +refill(lines): MachineView
  }
}

package "Startup configuration" {
  class MachineConfig <<Spring configuration>> {
    +vendingMachine(catalog, properties): VendingMachine
  }
  class MachineProperties <<configuration record>> {
    capacityPerSlot: int
    initialStockPerSlot: int
  }
  class ProductCatalog {
    +findAll(): List<Product>
    +find(id): Optional<Product>
  }
}

MachineController --> MachineService : delegates each route
MachineController ..> InsertCreditRequest
MachineController ..> PositionsRequest
MachineController ..> ReturnedCreditResponse
PositionsRequest *-- "1..*" CartItemRequest
MachineController ..> MachineView
MachineController ..> PurchaseResult
MachineExceptionHandler ..> MachineException : maps domain errors
MachineExceptionHandler ..> MachineError : selects HTTP status
MachineService --> VendingMachine : calls the aggregate
MachineConfig ..> ProductCatalog : reads fixed products
MachineConfig ..> MachineProperties : reads capacity and stock
MachineConfig ..> VendingMachine : creates the single bean

note bottom of MachineController
The controller converts validated JSON records
to domain values. The machine checks business
rules again; HTTP validation is not trusted alone.
end note

note bottom of MachineExceptionHandler
Errors become RFC 9457 problem details with
a stable code, status, request path and detail.
end note

note bottom of MachineConfig
The Spring container injects the configured
VendingMachine into MachineService at startup.
There is no database or persistence class.
end note
@enduml
